
@*
    The landing page presents the three architectural pillars of the
    Smart-X IoT Mesh Ecosystem using Bootstrap cards inside a responsive
    grid.

    Bootstrap's 12-column grid system is used through the row and
    col-md-4 classes to create a responsive three-column layout
    (Bootstrap, 2026e).

    Bootstrap card components are used to group the information for each
    architectural pillar, while Bootstrap buttons provide the interactive
    controls (Bootstrap, 2026d; Bootstrap, 2026c).

    The ASP.NET Core Anchor Tag Helper generates the appropriate links for
    the Sensor section using the controller and action names rather than
    requiring hard-coded URLs (Microsoft, 2026a).

    HTML elements are used to structure the page content and navigation
    areas (W3Schools, 2025b).

    Custom CSS is used to improve the visual presentation, spacing,
    responsiveness and appearance of the Bootstrap components
    (W3Schools, 2025a).

    The structured layout demonstrates the use of object-oriented and
    component-based programming concepts by separating the system into
    distinct functional areas (Nakov and Kolev et al., 2013;
    Troelsen and Japikse, 2022).
*@

@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Smart-X Gateway";
}

<style>

    /*
            Custom styling is used to improve the appearance of the landing
            page while retaining Bootstrap's responsive grid and card system
            (Bootstrap, 2026e; W3Schools, 2025a).
        */

    .smart-x-page {
        padding-top: 50px;
        padding-bottom: 50px;
    }

    .smart-x-header {
        text-align: center;
        margin-bottom: 45px;
    }

        .smart-x-header h1 {
            font-weight: 700;
            margin-bottom: 12px;
        }

        .smart-x-header p {
            color: #adb5bd;
            font-size: 1.05rem;
            margin-bottom: 0;
        }

    .architecture-card {
        height: 100%;
        min-height: 280px;
        border: 1px solid #343a40;
        border-radius: 16px;
        overflow: hidden;
        background-color: #1f2226;
        box-shadow: 0 6px 18px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.2);
        transition: transform 0.2s ease, box-shadow 0.2s ease;
    }

        .architecture-card:hover {
            transform: translateY(-5px);
            box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3);
        }

        .architecture-card .card-body {
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
            justify-content: center;
            align-items: center;
            text-align: center;
            padding: 32px 25px;
        }

    .architecture-icon {
        width: 58px;
        height: 58px;
        border-radius: 50%;
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        justify-content: center;
        margin-bottom: 20px;
        background-color: #2f8fdb;
        color: white;
        font-size: 1.4rem;
        font-weight: 700;
    }

    .architecture-card .card-title {
        font-weight: 600;
        margin-bottom: 15px;
        color: #f8f9fa;
    }

    .architecture-card .card-text {
        color: #adb5bd;
        line-height: 1.6;
        max-width: 360px;
        margin-bottom: 25px;
    }

    .architecture-card .btn {
        min-width: 120px;
        border-radius: 8px;
        font-weight: 600;
        padding: 9px 20px;
    }

    /*
            Disabled cards use a darker appearance to indicate that those
            system features are not currently available.
        */

    .architecture-card.disabled-card {
        background-color: #181a1d;
        opacity: 0.75;
    }

        .architecture-card.disabled-card:hover {
            transform: none;
            box-shadow: 0 6px 18px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.2);
        }

        .architecture-card.disabled-card .architecture-icon {
            background-color: #495057;
        }

        .architecture-card.disabled-card .card-title {
            color: #adb5bd;
        }

    .status-badge {
        display: inline-block;
        padding: 5px 10px;
        border-radius: 20px;
        background-color: #495057;
        color: #dee2e6;
        font-size: 0.75rem;
        font-weight: 600;
        margin-bottom: 18px;
    }

    .active-badge {
        background-color: #198754;
        color: white;
    }

</style>


<div class="container smart-x-page">

    <!--
        The Bootstrap container and grid provide a responsive structure for
        the landing page (Bootstrap, 2026e).
    -->

    <div class="smart-x-header">

        <h1>
            Smart-X IoT Mesh Ecosystem
        </h1>

        <p>
            Select an architectural pillar to continue
        </p>

    </div>


    <!--
        Bootstrap's row and column classes create the responsive three-card
        layout (Bootstrap, 2026e).
    -->

    <div class="row justify-content-center g-4">


        <!-- SENSOR DATA INGESTION -->

        <div class="col-md-4">

            <!--
                Bootstrap's card component is used to group the sensor
                ingestion functionality into a single visual section
                (Bootstrap, 2026d).
            -->

            <div class="card architecture-card">

                <div class="card-body">

                    <div class="architecture-icon">
                        01
                    </div>

                    <span class="status-badge active-badge">
                        AVAILABLE
                    </span>

                    <h4 class="card-title">
                        Sensor Data Ingestion &amp; Telemetry
                    </h4>

                    <p class="card-text">
                        Register sensors, ingest telemetry, and monitor
                        live sensor status.
                    </p>

                    <!--
                        The Anchor Tag Helper generates the appropriate
                        URL for the Sensors controller and Index action
                        (Microsoft, 2026a).
                    -->

                    <a asp-controller="Sensors"
                       asp-action="Index"
                       class="btn btn-success">
                        Enter
                    </a>

                </div>

            </div>

        </div>


        <!-- COMMAND STREAM -->

       <div class="col-md-4">

    <div class="card architecture-card">

        <div class="card-body">

            <div class="architecture-icon">
                02
            </div>

            <span class="status-badge active-badge">
                AVAILABLE
            </span>

            <h4 class="card-title">
                Real-Time Command Stream &amp; History
            </h4>

            <p class="card-text">
                Monitor live device data, issue manual override
                commands and review suggested actions.
            </p>

            <a asp-controller="CommandStream"
               asp-action="Index"
               class="btn btn-success">
                Enter
            </a>

        </div>

    </div>

</div>

                    <!--
                        Bootstrap button styling is used to communicate
                        that this functionality is currently unavailable
                        (Bootstrap, 2026c).
                    -->
        <!-- NETWORK TOPOLOGY -->

        <div class="col-md-4">

            <div class="card architecture-card">

                <div class="card-body">

                    <div class="architecture-icon">
                        03
                    </div>

                    <span class="status-badge active-badge">
                        AVAILABLE
                    </span>

                    <h4 class="card-title">
                        Network Topology &amp; Mesh Routing
                    </h4>

                    <p class="card-text">
                        View the mesh network, track the most power-efficient
                        route of a sensor to the gateway and search its
                        historical telemetry by time range.
                    </p>

                    <a asp-controller="Topology"
                       asp-action="Index"
                       class="btn btn-success">
                        Enter
                    </a>

                </div>

            </div>

        </div>


